  24:     Return the 3x3 monochrome sprite type that appears most often in the input.
  25: 
  26:     Input structure
  27:     The grid has a dominant background and several small monochrome foreground sprites.
  28:     Each sprite is an 8-connected component whose bounding box is 3x3.
  29: 
  30:     Rule
  31:     Normalize each sprite to its 3x3 bounding-box mask, keeping its color as part of
  32:     the sprite identity. Count identical colored sprite types and output one copy of
  33:     the uniquely most frequent type on the background.
  34: 
  35:     Key insight
  36:     The output is not a crop from a particular location; it is the repeated motif
  37:     selected by copy count.
